\section{Decorators}
\begin{note}
A \emph{decorator} is a function that takes a function and returns a function.
For example, we saw in a previous lab that \lstinline{lru_cache} is a decorator that \emph{memoizes} recursive functions to make them more efficient.
The syntax \lstinline{@decorate def f(x): ...}
is ``syntactic sugar'' for \lstinline{f = decorate(f)}.
Decorators can modify functions, classes, and any other object type in python.
\end{note}
